+## Kimi Code integration reference
+
+Kimi uses Codenotch's `KimiCredentials.swift`, `KimiProvider.swift` and `KimiUsage.swift` at the pinned reference commit above. It reads `credentials/kimi-code.json` under a nonempty `KIMI_CODE_HOME`, otherwise `~/.kimi-code` (the current user's home on Windows too). Require a nonempty `access_token` and a positive epoch-seconds `expires_at`. The file is read-only; Kimi Code CLI owns OAuth login and renewal. Expired credentials require CLI renewal, not an attempted supplier request or an independently refreshed token. Static Moonshot Platform API keys are not Kimi Code subscription credentials. The official [provider documentation](https://moonshotai.github.io/kimi-code/en/configuration/providers.html#oauth-and-credential-injection) confirms the managed OAuth login/renewal contract.
